<title>HONG KONG: Huaneng gets OK for power plant project.</title>
<headline>Huaneng gets OK for power plant project.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Huaneng Power International Inc said on Friday the Chinese government has approved all its power projects scheduled to be onstream by 2000.</p>
<p>On its planned Huaneng Dandong Power Plant, consisting two units of 350 megawatts each, all equipment would be financed by foreign loans, 85 percent with export credit from the United States and United Kingdom and 15 percent with a commercial loan.</p>
<p>The two units are expected to be onstream from 1998 and 1999, but the company's statement did not state where the plant would be sited. --HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 28436441</p>
</text>
